This code snippet defines a function `allocate_mac_pdus` that dynamically allocates memory for an array of `MAC_PDU` structures, ensuring each structure contains valid pointers to `PDCP_PDU`, `RLC_PDU`, and `PHY_PDU` with correctly initialized fields. It handles memory allocation failures gracefully by logging error messages and attempting to free any partially allocated resources before returning `NULL`. The function also initializes the structures and links them in a doubly linked list, maintaining the order and integrity of the data flow.']

